{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The trusted run reproduced the local discrepancy: replica 2 acknowledged Accept for instance (0,0), then reported status 2 under Prepare ballot 6. The identity, prerequisite and result events match. The accepted command and ordering attributes remained intact, so the evidence supports a phase-reporting defect, not yet a claim that recovery chose a conflicting value."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nr=json.load(open('../research.json')); aid=r['artifacts'][0]['id']; cid=r['candidates'][0]['id']; run=r['assessments'][0]['experiment_check_id']\nss=['S_init','S_base','S_propose','S_preaccept','S_fast','S_send','S_accept','S_accept_reply','S_prepare','S_recover_select','S_wire','S_try','S_recovery_trigger','S_start_recovery','S_transport','S_receive','S_rpc_codec','S_prepare_codec','S_preaccept_codec','S_client_types']\nrationale='''Reviewed fixed artifact fe4123fad9df42eaa262ca8e63173da3 v1, its fixed harness lines 25-129, O_accepted_phase_report v1, the retained raw stdout/stderr and CheckRun 60e27f33b9834b7d87fa2fe866557a2e. No correspondence issue was found for this local proposition. This is provisional semantic review, not proof beyond the witnessed scope.\n\nResponsibility and oracle: the request is admitted only when its ballot is not lower and the local instance is uncommitted (S_accept). Matching AcceptReply increments acceptance support at the coordinator (S_accept_reply). A later Prepare exposes stored Status, while recovery explicitly prioritizes ACCEPTED before preacceptance cases (S_prepare/S_recover_select). S_try 1357-1360 independently describes preserving accepted phase against regression. These composed local interfaces ground reporting ACCEPTED after acknowledged acceptance with no intervening value/phase change. The predicate compares the actual report.status to the declared ACCEPTED constant 3; it does not claim that unchanged attributes alone imply safety or require a quorum decision before each acceptor can retain acceptance. There is one checker and no unrelated test predicate.\n\nHistory and entry duties: constructor-equivalent fields match the relevant empty state, N=5/F=2, Thrifty, Dreply and non-durable defaults. Only row-0 slot 0 and row-1 slot 0 are used within the reduced capacities. Actual handlePropose starts both commands, not seeded accepted state. Distinct producer-generated preaccept replies carry Seq=1/Deps=[-1,0,-1,-1,-1] and Seq=-1/all-minus-one; real aggregation therefore emits the slow Accept. Fixed lines 96-105 check the coordinator phase, target identity, admission ballot/status and matching acknowledgment before allowing the prerequisite event. Its count=1 is the real coordinator counter, below commitment threshold; no client reply is required for this local endpoint. Nil client reply writers are unused because neither instance commits. All protocol payloads come through unchanged SendMsg and message codecs, decoded using registered New/Unmarshal. Receive consumes the next bytes on each directed link. The older row-1 proposal is delivered on 1->2 before the later Prepare, with its actual reply also consumed. It updates another instance and conflict indexes, not the target phase or value. Replica 1 already knows unresolved target (0,0) and its row horizon; a direct recovery event models the scanner callback for that eligible slot. No timer deadline or absence-of-progress claim is encoded. No recovery replies are delivered to selection, so recovery self-vbal effects cannot cause the observed acceptor phase result.\n\nObservation and correlation: the runner exited 0, target test completed, stderr is empty, and parsing_errors is empty. Raw CA_EVENT index 6 records acceptor 2, origin 0, instance 0, acknowledgment ballot 0 and coordinator_accept_count=1. Index 11 reports the same independent identity with promise 6 and status 2 (PREACCEPTED_EQ). The monitor admission_alias is accepted; its prerequisite is a genuine earlier acknowledgment, not a copy of the result. Status and changing ballots are not identity keys. Fixed lines 120-123 independently check the greater Prepare ballot and returned acceptor/origin/instance/context. The result is a newly decoded serialized reply read synchronously after handlePrepare returns. There are no concurrent workers or mutable observations racing with handlers. completed=true records actual attainment of this decode, not a readiness prediction. Handler return, buffer decode and normal test exit complete this proposition; no join, socket close, cancellation or client completion is needed for its local witness. Pending byte streams are the finite undelivered suffix of an asynchronous history, not worker cleanup or a fabricated permanent stall.\n\nMeasured result: the acknowledgment is followed by an actual status=2 report where this obligation requires 3. The raw reply still carries command target, Seq=1 and the accepted dependency vector, so value-content loss is not established. S_accept provides a direct source explanation: its admitted branch writes Deps/Seq/bal/vbal but never Status, and S_prepare forwards that retained Status. PrepareReply codec serializes Status faithfully; its independent VBallot omission does not affect this comparison at initial value ballot 0. The missing phase assignment explains this local result without attributing an unexecuted global consequence.'''\nitem=dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=ss,rationale=rationale,counterevidence=['Original coordinator has ACCEPTED state and another recovery participant might preserve the value.','Actual report retained the target command, Seq=1 and dependency vector; no conflicting decision was observed.'],limitations=['Only one producer-derived finite history and one local acceptor report are checked.','No PrepareReply is consumed by recovery selection in this check; full agreement and eventual continuation remain untested.','Network startup, execution goroutine and elapsed recovery timer are substituted by a serial handler schedule with known unresolved-slot eligibility.','PrepareReply VBallot serialization and recovery self-vbal mutation are independent unresolved mechanisms.'],challenged_components=[],report_title='Accept 已确认，恢复回复仍报告预接受状态',report_answer='五副本执行中，副本 2 确认实例